course: dictionary
lesson: 2024
title: Confident: sure of yourself, or sure it will happen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Confident means feeling sure that you can do something well, or sure that something will happen. «Ravi is a confident swimmer» means he feels sure he can swim well. «I'm confident we'll win» means the speaker feels sure the team will win.
explain: Use the words around it to choose the right meaning. Swimmer tells you the word is about ability, and «we'll win» tells you it is about what will happen. Read the sentence again with the clue in mind.
explain: Check your meaning with a swap: put sure in place of confident. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning. Confident also has an adverb, confidently, which means in a sure way, as in «She spoke confidently.»
explain: Confident often comes with a small word after it: confident about, confident that, confident in. You can also feel confident, or be self-confident, which means you believe in yourself. Confidence grows with practice, so making mistakes is part of getting there.
fact: Confident means feeling sure that you can do something well, as in a confident swimmer.
fact: Confident also means sure that something will happen or is true, as in «I'm confident that we'll win».
fact: Confidently is the adverb, and it means in a sure way.
fact: Confident is often followed by about, that or in: confident about a test, confident in your team.
fact: Confidence grows with practice, and making mistakes is part of learning.
exercise: «Being confident in water starts with small skills, like floating on your back.» What does confident mean here? | Tired from swimming | Scared of the water | Wet and cold | *Feeling sure that you can do something well
exercise: «I'm confident we'll win.» What does confident mean here? | *Sure that something will happen | Feeling sick | Not sure at all | Loud and bossy
exercise: Find the word that means in a sure way. | confuse | *confidently | confetti | confident
test: At school, teachers help pupils feel confident reading aloud. What does feel confident mean here? | Feel sleepy | Feel cold | Feel nervous about reading | *Feel sure that you can read well
test: Complete the sentence: I'm confident ___ the test. Which word fits best? | *about | across | under | into
exam: «Confident speakers still feel nervous; practising and starting with a smile help.» Which meaning fits confident here? | Very angry | Quiet and shy | *Sure of themselves when they speak, even if they still feel a little nervous | Never nervous at all
